# Code owners.
#
# Review here is not a formality. NEBULA's entire value is that ten
# implementations agree, so the files that define what "agree" means — the
# specification, the vectors, the compatibility contract — need an owner who
# will refuse a change that silently forks behaviour in one language.
#
# GitHub uses the LAST matching pattern, so the ordering below is
# general-to-specific on purpose.
#
# Every rule below names @nebula-token/maintainers, one team, because a team is
# the only owner form that survives a change in who the maintainers are: a second
# maintainer joins by being added to the team, and this file is not touched. A
# bare organization is NOT a valid owner — GitHub accepts @username or
# @org/team-name and nothing else — so @nebula-token on its own would resolve to
# nobody.
#
# THE TEAM MUST BE VISIBLE AND MUST HAVE EXPLICIT `write` ACCESS TO THIS
# REPOSITORY. Both, separately. A secret team is skipped, and a team whose
# members already have write access through the organization is still skipped
# unless the team itself was granted it. In either case GitHub does not fail:
# the rule matches, no review is requested, and the file goes on looking
# enforced. Check it on a real pull request before trusting branch protection.
#
# The per-path rows all point at that one team today. They are kept because they
# are the review boundaries this project considers real, and because splitting
# them across specialised teams later is a change to the owner column only.

# Everything, by default.
*                               @nebula-token/maintainers

# ------------------------------------------------------------ the contract
#
# A change here changes every implementation at once, whether or not the pull
# request touches them.

/SPECIFICATION.md               @nebula-token/maintainers
/spec/                          @nebula-token/maintainers
/COMPATIBILITY.md               @nebula-token/maintainers
/VERSIONING.md                  @nebula-token/maintainers
/SUPPORT.md                     @nebula-token/maintainers

